    "result_text": "All 260 tests pass, including the new `AcceptanceTest`. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `membershipTier` to become `'GOLD'` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3 or more members after creation, otherwise falling back to the existing BRONZE/SILVER rules.\n\n**Key insight:** The tier was previously computed entirely in `OwnerMapper.formatMembershipTier`, which sees only a single `Owner` and has no repository access \u2014 so it can't count household members. GOLD requires counting other owners, which needs the `ClinicService`. The controller is the right place: it already post-processes the mapped DTO (e.g. for `bulkSignupWarning`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipTier(Owner)` helper that counts owners sharing the owner's non-null `householdId`; returns `\"GOLD\"` when the count is \u2265 3, otherwise delegates to `ownerMapper.formatMembershipTier(owner)` (the unchanged BRONZE/SILVER rule). Applied it in both `getOwner` and `addOwner` after mapping, via `ownerDto.setMembershipTier(...)`.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` field description to document the GOLD rule ahead of SILVER/BRONZE.\n\nThe existing household-linking logic in `addOwner` already assigns a shared `householdId` to all same-household members, so after the third member is created all three carry the same id and the count reaches 3 \u2192 GOLD. The BRONZE/SILVER logic in the mapper is untouched, so owners without a household (null `householdId`) can never be GOLD and keep their prior tier.",
